// ch09 (round 2, R2-5; re-aimed for ADR-0088's entry rule): `allows` is the
// GRANT of an entry point and may not sit on a called function -- a called
// function requires with `with`. The book quotes the diagnostic; measure that
// it still matches. Note the real prefix is `error: line 1:1:` with NO file
// path -- the only diagnostic round 2 met without one.
fn greet(name: String) -> Unit allows Console {
  println("hi \{name}")
}

fn main allows Console {
  greet("vibe")
}
